{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.BindingScaleCatalan","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.BindingScaleCatalan","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BindingScale.bindingScale_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BindingScale.bindingScale_value","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-scale-catalan.lean#L29-L38","doc":"The binding scale is `8G` times the electron scale, for every value of\n`m_e`. No measured value enters the statement: evaluating at the CODATA\nelectron mass (`α ≈ 3.7445 MeV`) is the comparison boundary of\n`conj:binding-scale-catalan`, not part of it. This proves the\n`Vol(B₃) = 8G` factorisation only; the identification of `bindingScale`\nwith the binding correction of the atomic mass formula is the conjecture. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:binding-scale-catalan","label":"conj:binding-scale-catalan","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-scale-catalan.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BindingScale.bindingScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BindingScale.bindingScale","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-scale-catalan.lean#L26-L27","doc":"The binding energy scale connects lepton mass to baryon topology. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BindingScale.volBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BindingScale.volBorromean","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-scale-catalan.lean#L20-L24","doc":"Volume of the Borromean rings complement = 8G.\nThis is a theorem of hyperbolic geometry:\nthe complement decomposes into 2 regular ideal octahedra,\neach of volume 4G. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BindingScale.catalanConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BindingScale.catalanConstant","kind":"def","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-scale-catalan.lean#L15-L18","doc":"Catalan's constant G = Σ (-1)^k / (2k+1)².\nMigrate to `Real.catalan` once it lands in Mathlib. ","signatureChunk":0}]}